Every family in Nairobi County deserves quality healthcare close to home. As Governor, Bill Llia will make healthcare access the top priority of his administration — not as a slogan, but as a funded, measurable commitment.

**A health center in every ward:** Within 18 months of taking office, every ward in Nairobi County will have a fully equipped community health center staffed by qualified nurses and clinical officers. No resident should travel more than 30 minutes to access primary care. We will partner with the national government and development partners to fast-track construction and renovation, with clear timelines published for every ward.

**Ending drug stock-outs for good:** Bill will implement a transparent, county-wide drug procurement and distribution system — using real-time inventory tracking — that ensures essential medicines are always available at public health facilities. No more mothers being turned away because the pharmacy is empty. No more treatable illnesses becoming emergencies.

**Maternal and child health:** Bill is committing to a target of zero preventable maternal deaths in county health facilities within his first term. This means 24-hour staffing of maternity wings, ambulances stationed in every constituency for emergency referrals, and a network of community health workers who can reach every pregnant woman in the county with antenatal and postnatal care.

**Universal health coverage access:** We will organize quarterly health insurance enrollment drives in every ward, in partnership with the National Hospital Insurance Fund, to ensure that every family in Nairobi County has coverage. No family will be denied care because they cannot afford to pay at the point of service.

Bill Llia has spent his career in healthcare. He knows that prevention saves lives and money. He will fight for a system that keeps Nairobi County healthy — not one that waits until people get sick.
